UPDATE companies SET description='Stengel Bros. Inc. operates from Whitehall Township, Pennsylvania. The company has been in business for over 43 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The company distributes a broad range of suspension components including leaf springs, air ride suspensions, lift axles, truck bumpers, shock absorbers, coil springs, helper kits, trailer axles, U-bolts, and wheel centering products. It carries parts from name‑brand manufacturers such as Monroe, Goodyear, Link Manufacturing, Reyco Granning, Hendrickson, Watson & Chalin, and others. Stengel Bros. also offers custom U‑bolt fabrication for non‑standard applications and ships replacement air springs and heavy‑duty springs nationwide via UPS.

The catalog references specific applications for Mack, Peterbilt, Kenworth, Volvo, Freightliner, International, and Navistar trucks; Reyco, Neway, Fruehauf, Hutch, and Trailmobile trailer suspensions; and Ford, Chevrolet, GMC, Dodge, Toyota, Nissan, Mitsubishi, and Mazda light trucks and SUVs.

Stengel Bros. emphasizes its longevity — over four decades in the industry — and a guarantee on all parts and services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Leaf spring distribution", "Suspension part distribution", "Air ride suspension distribution", "Lift axle distribution", "Truck bumper distribution", "Shock absorber distribution", "Coil spring distribution", "Helper spring kit distribution", "Trailer axle distribution", "U-bolt custom fabrication", "Wheel centering product distribution", "Suspension air valve and control distribution", "Tire pressure monitoring system distribution", "Steering component distribution"], "industries": ["Commercial trucking", "Trailer manufacturing and repair", "Automotive aftermarket (light truck/SUV)", "RV and motorhome", "Utility trailer"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Location: Whitehall Township, Pennsylvania -> db", "Business duration: over 43 years -> /", "Product range: leaf springs, suspension parts, air ride suspensions, lift axles, bumpers, shocks -> /", "Brands carried: Monroe, Goodyear, Link Mfg, Reyco Granning, Hendrickson, Watson & Chalin -> /", "Industries served: medium/heavy duty trucks, trailers, light trucks, RVs -> /", "Custom U-bolts made to order -> /", "Nationwide UPS shipping on air springs -> /", "Parts and services guaranteed -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Stengel Bros. Inc. offers quality leaf springs, suspension parts, and air ride suspensions by name brand manufactures.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stengel-bros-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sterling Furniture Company has operated in Salt Lake City, Utah, since 1875, when master cabinet maker Hans Madsen opened a store on Main Street. The business remains family-owned, now directed by seventh-generation descendants of Madsen, and its flagship location has anchored the Sugar House neighborhood since 1941.

The company retails home furnishings across living room, bedroom, dining room, and office categories, offering customers the ability to customize fabric selections on special orders at no extra charge. It maintains three display floors at its Sugar House showroom and provides delivery throughout the Salt Lake Valley.

Its inventory emphasizes hardwood construction and traditional joinery, with a focus on accessible pricing and flexible payment terms that echo the founder''s original installment approach.

The Madsen family frames its differentiation around generational expertise in selecting durable materials and time-honored construction methods, positioning the store as a source for furniture intended to last across generations rather than follow short-lived trends.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabric selection", "Furniture delivery", "Special order customization"], "industries": ["Home furnishings", "Residential furniture retail"], "materials": ["Hardwoods", "Fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Special orders at no extra cost", "Free delivery within Salt Lake Valley", "Seven generations of family ownership", "Customizable fabric selection"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1875 by Hans Madsen -> /about", "Family-owned, seventh generation -> /about", "Headquarters Salt Lake City, Utah (Sugar House) -> /about", "Retails home furnishings with customizable fabric -> /, /services", "Offers free delivery in Salt Lake Valley -> /services", "Special orders at no extra cost -> /services", "Emphasis on hardwood construction and joinery -> /quality", "Purpose: quality furnishings at flexible pricing -> /about"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We have provided residents of the Wasatch Front a wide range of high quality, customized furniture at accessible prices.", "founded_year": "1875", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sterling-furniture-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sterling Wire & Cable operates from Minneapolis, Minnesota, where it serves as a wire and cable specialist. The company stocks over 15,000 wire and cable products, including categories such as data and communications cable, building wire, hook-up and lead wire, broadcast and AV cable, electronic cable, fire alarm cable, and safety, sound, and security cable. It also offers value-added services: custom cable design, dyeing and striping (28–10 AWG, 1–2 day lead time), custom respooling and coiling, cut-and-strip services, cut-and-labeled tubing, twisting (28–12 AWG, 1–2 week lead time), consolidated shipments, same-day shipping for orders placed before noon, vendor-managed inventory programs, UL/CSA repackaging, and full traceability to the original manufacturer. Sterling serves industries that require specialized cabling, such as access control systems (evidenced by 3M-approved and Solventum-approved cables), data communications, building infrastructure, broadcast and AV, electronics, fire alarm, and security. The company emphasizes on-time delivery, competitive pricing, and collaborative innovation to create reliable solutions. Differentiators highlighted by Sterling include same-day shipping on stock items, vendor-managed inventory programs, UL and CSA certification for repackaging, and full product traceability.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','ISO 9001','UL','CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable design and manufacturing", "Dyeing and striping (28\u201310 AWG)", "Custom respooling and coiling", "Cut and strip services", "Cut and labeled tubing", "Twisting (28\u201312 AWG)", "Consolidated shipments", "Same-day shipping", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) programs", "UL/CSA repackaging", "Full traceability", "Line card reference"], "industries": ["Data & Communications", "Building Wire", "Hook-up & Lead Wire", "Broadcast & AV", "Electronic Cable", "Fire Alarm", "Safety, Sound & Security", "Access Control Systems"], "m