UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2020, Stickbulb operates a 10,000-square-foot showroom, studio, and workshop inside a converted century-old iron factory in Long Island City, New York. The company is organized as Stickbulb LLC and combines design, prototyping, and production under one roof.

Stickbulb designs and manufactures LED light fixtures using salvaged wood sourced from New York City''s urban forest — demolition sites, dismantled water towers, and fallen trees, often within a mile or two of the facility. The product line includes modular collections such as Pillar, Pleat, Skybang, Branching Bough, Ray, Chime, and Diamond, offered in standard sizes with custom lengths and configurations. Production relies on local vendors and flat-pack engineering to minimize shipping volume.

The company serves architects, lighting designers, and interior designers on residential and commercial projects across North America. Notable installations include the Copake Lake House in upstate New York (Desai Chia Architecture), the SoLo House in British Columbia (Perkins & Will), the GL1 project (RUX Studios), and 100 Norfolk in Manhattan (ODA). Stickbulb also supplies trade professionals through showrooms and agents.

Stickbulb positions its differentiation around climate-conscious manufacturing. It has been Climate Neutral certified since 2020, tracking, reducing, and offsetting emissions, and became a Certified B Corporation in 2022. The hyper-local supply chain diverts old-growth timber from landfills, while modular flat-pack designs lower the carbon footprint of distribution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["LED fixture design and manufacturing", "Salvaged wood milling and finishing", "Modular lighting system engineering", "Custom lighting fabrication", "Architectural lighting specification support", "3D modeling and spec sheet provision", "Material sampling program", "Flat-pack assembly design"], "industries": ["Architectural lighting", "Interior design", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Trade professionals (architects, lighting designers, interior designers)"], "materials": ["Salvaged old-growth timber (NYC demolitions)", "Reclaimed water tower redwood", "Reclaimed heart pine", "Ebonized oak", "Walnut", "Kozo Japanese paper (mulberry bark)", "Brushed brass", "Polished nickel", "Matte black metal", "White metal", "Steel (slumped steel rings)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Climate Neutral certified since 2020", "B Corp certified since 2022", "Hyper-local wood sourcing from NYC demolitions within 1\u20132 miles", "Modular flat-pack design reduces shipping volume", "Integrated 10,000 sq ft showroom, studio, and workshop in historic iron factory"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020 -> db", "HQ Long Island City, NY -> db", "10,000 sq ft facility in converted iron factory -> /", "Showroom, studio, workshop in same building -> /", "Climate Neutral certified since 2020 -> /", "B Corp certified 2022 -> /", "Salvaged wood from NYC demolitions, water towers, fallen trees -> /", "Hyper-local sourcing within 1-2 miles -> /", "Modular flat-pack designs -> /", "Product collections: Pillar, Pleat, Skybang, Branching Bough, Ray, Chime, Diamond -> /", "Custom lengths and configurations -> /", "Served architects, lighting designers, interior designers -> /", "Project examples: Copake Lake House, SoLo House, GL1, 100 Norfolk -> /", "Materials: reclaimed redwood, heart pine, ebonized oak, walnut, Kozo paper, brass, nickel, steel -> /", "Stickbulb LLC copyright 2023 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LED fixture manufacturer with showroom, studio, and workshop in a converted iron factory", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stickbulb' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sticks, Inc. was founded in 1992 in West Des Moines, Iowa. The company began as a studio creating one-of-a-kind handmade art and furniture, with each piece drawn, wood-burned, and painted by artisan hands.

Today Sticks operates a production studio in Des Moines where it manufactures a wide range of home furnishings and accessories, including sculptures, wall plaques, lamps, lazy Susans, furniture such as tables, chairs, beds, and case goods, as well as holiday ornaments and custom heirloom pieces. The process remains entirely handcrafted: designs are hand-drawn, wood-burned, and hand-painted. The company also runs the Sticks Gallery in Des Moines’ Historic East Village, a retail destination opened in 2002 that carries the full Sticks line alongside work from over 150 other American makers.

Sticks serves both direct consumers and the trade. Collections span bedroom, dining, entryway, kitchen, living room, and office categories, with themed lines such as Americana, Lake, Mountain, Wine, and Wedding/Anniversary.

The company’s stated distinction is its commitment to storytelling through art: every piece is created from start to finish by artisans in the Des Moines studio, and the custom program lets customers commission furniture and accessories inspired by personal stories, places, or family history. This emphasis on narrative-driven, American-made craftsmanship has defined the brand since its inception.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand drawing", "Wood burning", "Hand painting", "Custom furniture design", "Custom accessory design", "Wholesale order fulfillment", "Retail gallery management", "Installation services"], "industries": ["Home furnishings", "Home decor", "Giftware", "Art", "Wholesale", "Retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> db", "Headquarters West Des Moines, Iowa -> db", "Studio in Des Moines -> /", "Gallery in Historic East Village since 2002 -> /", "Handmade process: drawn, wood-burned, painted by hand -> /", "Custom heirloom design service -> /", "Wholesale program -> /", "Over 150 other American artists showcased -> /", "Product categories: furniture, accessories, sculptures, ornaments, etc. -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sticks Handmade pieces are all one-of-a-kind and created by artisan hands from start to finish. Art & furniture made in America since 1992.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sticks-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Stitch N Print, Inc. has operated in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma since its founding in 1974. The company has served the local market and surrounding areas for decades, building a reputation for custom decorated apparel and textile products.

The shop provides a range of decoration services including screen printing (up to seven colors on items such as shirts, jackets, hats, bags, tablecloths, towels, notebooks, and umbrellas), embroidery on similar substrates, team uniform assembly with trim and piping, direct-to-garment printing, sewn banners, vinyl lettering and numbering, and tackle twill custom lettering and numbering.

