UPDATE companies SET description='Streamline Plastics operates from Ogden, Utah, where it was founded in 1990 as a family-owned business. The company has remained under family ownership for over three decades, building its reputation on consistent quality and dependable timelines.

The shop provides plastic injection molding, blow molding, and a range of secondary services including part and mold design, mold building, packaging and assembly, kitting, bottle filling, and fulfillment. Its capabilities cover injection packaging, handled bottles in sizes such as 2.5‑gallon and 2.5‑gallon XL, and full fulfillment operations from kitting to shipping.

Customers include manufacturers who need reliable supply of molded components and finished goods; testimonials cite senior buyers, procurement directors, and sales directors who rely on Streamline for production-line parts, packaging, and assembled products. The company serves clients seeking to reduce inventory carrying costs and avoid production shutdowns caused by long lead times.

Streamline emphasizes clear communication throughout every project phase, transparent tracking from order to delivery, and quick turnaround times as its core differentiators. The firm positions itself as a partner that eliminates miscommunication, costly rework, and unpredictable supply chains.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Blow Molding", "Part & Mold Design", "Mold Building", "Packaging & Assembly", "Injection Packaging", "Handled Bottles", "2.5 Gallon/2.5 Gallon XL", "Fulfillment", "Kitting", "Bottle Filling"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1990", "Clear communication throughout the entire process", "On-time delivery with transparent tracking", "Tailored designs with regular updates", "Quick turnaround times"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990, family-owned -> db, /", "Headquarters Ogden, Utah -> db, /", "Services: Injection Molding, Blow Molding, Fulfillment, Part & Mold Design, Mold Building, Packaging & Assembly, Injection Packaging, Handled Bottles, 2.5 Gallon/2.5 Gallon XL, Kitting, Bottle Filling -> /", "Differentiators: clear communication, transparent tracking, tailored designs, quick turnaround -> /", "Customer types: senior buyer, director of procurement/R&D, director of sales -> /", "Testimonials referencing reduced inventory, production-line supply, assembly of molded parts and packaging -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Plastic Injection Molding, Blow Molding, and Fulfillment.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='streamline-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Stromberg Metal Works, Inc. has operated from Beltsville, Maryland since 1940. The company began as a supplier for professional contractors across the East Coast and remains employee-owned and operated. Over more than seven decades it has expanded to four locations throughout Maryland, serving the Washington, D.C., Maryland, Virginia, and Pennsylvania region.

The firm provides metal design, fabrication, installation, and service for sheet metal and structural projects. Its shop capabilities include fully automated coil lines, plasma cutting tables, seam/MIG/TIG welding, mitre folding, cut-to-length processing, and in-house powder coating and paint booths. The company also produces spiral ductwork, Quikduc flange systems, coated ductwork, custom UL-rated boxes, and architectural ornamental metalwork. Engineering support covers shop drawings, automated estimation, and CAD drafting.

Stromberg specializes in laboratory, cleanroom, pharmaceutical, and data-center HVAC systems, where coated and spiral ductwork meet stringent airflow and corrosion requirements. The company also supplies architectural metal components such as custom hoods, panels, trim, and grilles for building envelopes and interior finishes.

