UPDATE companies SET description='The business unit focuses on surgical safety and education, though its founding year and ownership details are not publicly disclosed in the provided materials.

The unit develops and manufactures a portfolio of devices for the operating room, labor and delivery, and gastrointestinal suites. Key product lines include the SafeAir smoke evacuation system, SurgiCount+ and Triton for sponge counting and quantitative blood loss management, Neptune S and Neptune 3 fluid waste management systems with Smart Docking Stations, the PhotonBlade advanced monopolar energy platform, the POM procedural oxygen mask, and the Cactus smart sink system. The company also operates a Medical Education division that runs a Mobile Experience Lab and sponsors grants and scholarships through organizations such as AORN and AWHONN.

The company cites engagement with thousands of clinicians through 55 mobile experience stops, 240 regional sales-rep-led events, and participation in 10 national trade shows in 2025, along with sponsorship of AORN Expo grants and AWHONN obstetric patient safety scholarships.

Stryker Surgical Technologies frames its differentiation around a "Journey to Zero" aspiration targeting zero splashes and spills, zero surgical smoke, zero retained sponges, zero maternal harm, zero hypoxic injuries, and zero lost polyps. The company states that its commitment to nurse development through education and collaborative learning communities is central to its mission.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Smoke evacuation", "Sponge counting and quantitative blood loss management", "Fluid waste management", "Advanced monopolar energy delivery", "Procedural oxygen delivery and capnography", "Smart sink fluid management", "Medical education and training", "Mobile clinical experience labs"], "industries": ["Operating Room", "Labor & Delivery", "GI Suite", "Medical Education"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SafeAir", "SurgiCount+", "Triton", "Neptune S", "Smart Docking Station", "PhotonBlade", "Neptune 3", "POM", "Cactus"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Journey to Zero aspirational safety targets (zero splashes, smoke, retained sponges, maternal harm, hypoxic injuries, lost polyps)", "Mobile Experience Lab for hands-on clinical education", "AORN RSI Center of Excellence program sponsorship", "AWHONN Visionary Strategic Alliance membership", "Comprehensive surgical safety product portfolio spanning energy, waste management, and visualization"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Irvine, California -> db", "Product lines: SafeAir, SurgiCount+, Triton, Neptune S, PhotonBlade, Neptune 3, POM, Cactus -> page /", "Journey to Zero aspirational goals (zero splashes, smoke, retained sponges, maternal harm, hypoxic injuries, lost polyps) -> page /", "Medical education initiatives: Mobile Experience Lab, AORN grants, AWHONN scholarships -> page /", "2025 highlights: 55 mobile experience stops, 240 regional events, 10 national trade shows -> page /", "Industries served: operating room, labor & delivery, GI suite ->