UPDATE companies SET description='Sugar Hollow Solar is based in Asheville, North Carolina, and was founded in 2010 by cousins Doug Ager and Phelps Clarke. The company traces its roots to four generations of land stewardship in the southern Appalachians, with the founders having grown up on the family farm along Sugar Hollow Road in Fairview.

The firm provides full-service solar energy solutions, including design, installation, and maintenance of photovoltaic systems, battery backup storage, and electric-vehicle charging equipment.

Its customers span residential homeowners, commercial property owners, and nonprofit organizations seeking to reduce energy costs and carbon emissions. The company has installed systems for private homes, businesses, and community-focused nonprofits throughout the region.

Sugar Hollow distinguishes itself through its B Corp certification and membership in the Amicus Solar Cooperative, reflecting a commitment to social and environmental responsibility. The founders'' stated mission is to transition the Southern Appalachian community to clean energy with honesty, reliability, and expertise, prioritizing long-term relationships over short-term profit.', certifications=ARRAY['B Corp']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design", "Solar panel installation", "Battery backup system installation", "EV charging station installation", "System maintenance and repair", "Energy assessment and consulting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Nonprofit"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Battery storage systems", "EV charging equipment"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["B Corp certified business", "Member-owner of Amicus Solar Cooperative", "Largest local solar installer in Western NC and Upstate SC", "Over 1,000 solar and battery backup systems installed"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 by Doug Ager and Phelps Clarke -> db and /about-us", "Headquartered in Asheville, North Carolina -> db", "50+ employees -> /about-us", "Over 1,000 projects installed -> / and /about-us", "B Corp certified -> / and /about-us", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperative -> / and /about-us", "Services: solar panel installation, battery backup, EV charger installation -> /about-us", "Industries served: residential, commercial, nonprofit -> /about-us", "Largest local installer in Western NC and Upstate SC -> / and /about-us", "Voted Best Place to Work 2023 -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Today, as the largest local installer of solar panels and battery backup systems in Western North Carolina and Upstate South Carolina", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "50+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sugar-hollow-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Suminoe Textile of America (STA) is a wholly owned subsidiary of Suminoe Textile Ltd., a Japanese company with roots in Osaka dating back over 125 years. STA began operations in April 2003 at a purpose-built manufacturing facility in Gaffney, South Carolina, placing it in the heart of the Carolina textile corridor where it draws on the area''s deep pool of textile expertise.

The company produces automobile interior furnishings at full scale for the North American market, focusing on seat fabrics, floor mats, and carpets. Its finishing capabilities include printing, etching, napping, and sueding, applied to automotive textile substrates to meet OEM specifications.

Its product lineup centers on automotive fabrics and carpet systems for passenger vehicles, with all production occurring at its Gaffney plant.

