ral Valley -> /", "In-house teams, no subcontractors -> /", "$0 down financing -> /", "GAF Timberline HDZ RS roofing used in donation -> /about-us", "Commercial solar donation to worship center -> /about-us", "Roof donation to Faith Community Church -> /about-us", "Community donations: One Fresno Foundation, LLS, Blue Star Mothers, women''s organizations -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We install high-performance roofing systems built to last\u2014no subcontractors, just certified experts and strong manufacturer-backed warranties.", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunmade-smart-roofing-solar-fresno-electric' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunlight Solar Energy, Inc. is based in Bend, Oregon, and has been installing grid-tied solar electric systems across Central Oregon since approximately 2000. The company was founded by Paul Israel, who began his solar career in the late 1980s and launched a solar contracting business in Redmond in the late 1990s before moving operations to Bend. Israel was among the first licensed Renewable Energy Technicians in Oregon, and Sunlight Solar became the third Solar Trade Ally designated by the Energy Trust of Oregon.

The firm provides turn-key solar services including system design, permitting, installation, inspection, and utility interconnection for residential and commercial customers. Its in-house crews also install battery storage systems such as Tesla Powerwall, EV chargers, and smart electrical panels from Span and Eaton. The company maintains a dedicated service department for long-term maintenance and operates across Central Oregon communities including Bend, Redmond, Sisters, and surrounding areas.

Customers range from homeowners and small businesses to municipal clients and affordable-housing developers. Notable projects include a 200.6 kW installation for Central Electric Cooperative, a 35 kW system for the Bend Centennial Parking Plaza, solar for the Oregon Department of Veteran Affairs, and partnerships with Central Oregon Habitat for Humanity, Rooted Homes, and Thistle and Nest. The team also handles commercial installations for clients such as Worthy Brewing and CiEs Inc.

Sunlight Solar emphasizes its local roots as a differentiator, stating that deep knowledge of regional permitting, utility requirements, and climate conditions allows it to build systems that perform reliably over decades. The company highlights honest quoting, clear communication, and customer education as core values, with the same personnel managing projects from initial design through ongoing service.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP certified','Energy Trust of Oregon Trade Ally','Tesla Powerwall certified installer','SolarEdge certified','Enphase certified','Oregon Journeyman Electrician license','Oregon Solar Electrician license','Oregon Racker license','OSHA 30 certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Permitting and interconnection", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Battery storage installation (Tesla Powerwall)", "EV charger installation", "Smart panel installation (Span, Eaton)", "Solar maintenance and service", "Municipal PV project development", "Solar financing coordination"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Municipal government", "Affordable housing", "Electric vehicle infrastructure", "Energy storage"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Lithium-ion battery systems", "Power inverters", "Racking and mounting systems", "Electrical distribution equipment"], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall", "Span smart panels", "Eaton smart panels", "SolarEdge inverters", "Enphase microinverters", "ChargePoint EV chargers"], "volume": "50+ residential and 5+ commercial/municipal projects per year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house licensed crews manage design, permitting, installation, and interconnection", "Same team handles projects from quote through long-term service", "Deep local knowledge of Central Oregon permitting, utilities, and climate", "Energy Trust of Oregon Trade Ally enabling customer rebate access", "NABCEP-certified installers and manufacturer-certified for Tesla, SolarEdge, Enphase"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bend, Oregon -> db", "Founded by Paul Israel, started grid-tied solar around 2000 -> /about-us", "Paul Israel background: first LRT in Oregon, third ETO Trade Ally, 40+ years experience -> /about-us", "Services: design, permit, install, interconnect, battery, EV, smart panels, maintenance -> /", "Service areas: Bend, Culver, La Pine, Madras, Prineville, Redmond, Sisters, Sunriver, Terrebonne, Tumalo, Warm Springs -> /", "Certifications: NABCEP, ETO Trade Ally, Tesla Powerwall, SolarEdge, Enphase, Span, ChargePoint -> /about-us", "Licensed Oregon Journeyman Electricians, Solar Electricians, Rackers -> /", "Notable projects: Central Electric Cooperative 200.6 kW, Bend Centennial Parking Plaza 35 kW, Oregon Dept of Veteran Affairs, Worthy Brewing, CiEs Inc. -> /", "Community partners: Habitat for Humanity, Rooted Homes, Thistle and Nest -> /about-us", "Awards: Best of Central Oregon (Source Weekly), Energy Installer of the Year (ETO) -> /about-us", "Joe Mazzarella: 50+ residential and 5+ commercial/municipal projects per year since 2011 -> /about-us", "Robert Johnson: joined 2001, Journeyman 2004, Signing Supervisor, OSHA 30 -> /about-us", "Company values: honesty, professionalism, education, community -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "As one of the few solar installers in Central Oregon with deep local roots, we handle every stage of a project ourselves: system design, permitting, installation, inspection, and utility interconnection.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunlight-solar-energy-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SunMED Medical Solutions was founded in 2002 in Marlton, New Jersey, as a provider of advanced in-home medical equipment and superior patient support. The company, led by President Bill Lobosco, began with a focus on delivering specialized equipment directly to patients'' homes while managing the complex insurance claims process.

Today SunMED operates nationwide as a diversified durable medical equipment (DME) provider and claims specialist. Its service lines include lymphedema therapy support, wound care therapy (covering negative-pressure wound therapy and compression wound care), women''s health (post-surgical garments and new-mother support), and a Supplier National Access Program (S.N.A.P.) that helps medical suppliers establish a national footprint. The company also administers the Wellcare for Women group benefit for employers. SunMED''s support staff functions as product and claims subject-matter experts rather than order takers, handling insurance verification, benefit maximization, and patient guidance.

The company serves patients, referring clinicians, therapists, medical suppliers, and employers across the home healthcare, wound care, lymphedema management, and women''s health markets. Clinicians rely on SunMED to deliver prescribed products and navigate reimbursement, while suppliers use the S.N.A.P. platform to access national distribution. Employers adopt Wellcare for Women as a voluntary benefit.

SunMED differentiates itself by maintaining a live, telephone-based support team at a time when many competitors have shifted to online-only administration. The firm states that its core purpose is "next-level service," emphasizing personal interaction and claims expertise to capture every eligible health coverage benefit for patients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["In-home medical equipment delivery", "Insurance claims processing and benefit verification", "Lymphedema therapy equipment support", "Negative-pressure wound therapy support", "Compression wound care support", "Post-surgical garment fitting and supply", "New mother support services", "Supplier national access program (S.N.A.P.)", "Employer group benefit administration (Wellcare for Women)", "Clinician and therapist support services"], "industries": ["Home healthcare", "Durable medical equipment (DME)", "Lymphedema therapy", "Wound care", "Women''s health", "Post-surgical care", "Maternity care"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Live telephone support staffed by product and claims experts, not automated online-only administration", "Nationwide in-home delivery and insurance claims management for DME", "Supplier National Access Program (S.N.A.P.) enabling medical suppliers to reach national markets", "Wellcare for Women group benefit program for employers", "Over 16 years of specialized experience in negative-pressure wound therapy and compression wound care"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 -> db", "Headquarters Marlton, New Jersey -> db", "President Bill Lobosco -> page ''/''", "Provider of advanced in-home medical equipment and superior support -> page ''/''", "Services expanded nationwide, premier national medical equipment claims experts -> page ''/''", "Live telephone support staff as product and claims subject matter experts -> page ''/''", "Lymphedema Therapy Support -> page ''/''", "Wound Care Therapy Sup