UPDATE companies SET description='Synteen Technical Fabrics was founded in 1998 in Lancaster, South Carolina. Initially serving the southeastern United States, the company expanded its reach across North America, Mexico, and the Caribbean. In a recent strategic move, Synteen was acquired by Maccaferri, Inc., a global construction and infrastructure group, while continuing to manufacture its products domestically in the United States.

The company operates a 40,000-square-foot facility where it produces uniaxial geogrids, biaxial geogrids, and high-strength woven fabrics. A team with over 75 years of combined experience oversees rigorous testing, continuous innovation, and responsiveness to customer feedback to maintain product quality and performance.

Synteen serves the geosynthetics industry, supplying solutions for civil construction, industrial construction, and infrastructure projects.

