UPDATE companies SET description='Tallapoosa River Electric Cooperative (TREC) was established in 1939 and is headquartered in LaFayette, Alabama. The cooperative operates as a not-for-profit, member-owned utility governed by a democratically elected board of trustees. It serves members across Clay, Randolph, Tallapoosa, Chambers, Lee, Russell, and Barbour counties in east-central Alabama.

Beyond power delivery, the cooperative provides free energy audits, free residential power quality audits, and free HVAC design assistance. It maintains multiple office locations in LaFayette, Fort Mitchell, Smith Station, Mellow Valley, and New Site, along with authorized payment drop boxes at Auburn Bank branches.

TREC also supports community initiatives such as the Rural Electric Cooperative Youth Tour, which offers high school juniors scholarships and trips to Montgomery and Washington, D.C.

